  "obligation": "Allocate custom-descriptor structs in bodies and constant expressions, retaining original descriptor identity, exact type ownership, payload roots and typed null traps; project ref.get_desc through the same shared VM.",
  "representation": "StructConstruction owns regular/default/described/default-described operator projections. The original WasmTypes graph derives descriptor types; one existing WasmGc cell owns optional descriptor and fields. Constant expressions admit the same construction modes and never fold allocation identity. Complete constructor windows include the descriptor as their final operand and derive root/validation behavior from the shared operand layout. Registration checks declaration, defaultability and exact window arity; execution checks original descriptor type before allocation. Descriptor projection checks the source owner/subtype, returns the stored original reference and traps on null. Heap tracing follows descriptor and field edges. Three opcodes append; format68 rejects old encodings without changing packed widths. No side registry, cell kind or executor is added.",
